sec.p:
Item-level descriptives and missing data information are provided in Supplemental Table. The overall rate of missing data was low (0.8%), with individual item missingness ranging from 0.7% (e.g. item 6) to 6.1% (item 9). The missingness pattern was primarily item-specific, with the majority of missing data (~ 52%) concentrated in two items (item 9 and item 21), likely due to their sensitive content. Regarding item-level acceptability, item means ranged from 1.60 to 3.14, and standard deviations ranged from 0.91 to 1.24, indicating no substantial floor or ceiling effects and sufficient variability across all items. Bartlett’s test of sphericity showed a significant result (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
