                                                  \begin{document}$$\:{\upchi\:}$$\end{document}2(351) = 2544.95, p < .001). The overall Kaiser-Meyer-Olkin measure (0.90) also indicated that the data were suitable for factor analysis. Due to the sensitivity of Bartlett’s test of sphericity to non-normally distributed data, the anti-image matrices for each item were additionally checked for values < 0.5, with only values ≥ 0.67 (item 18) being found overall. The sampling adequacy indices therefore supported the suitability of the data for exploratory factor analysis. For an overview of descriptive statistics per item/subscale, see Supplemental Table 1.

